.\" lscore-install-marker:0d3f5a1c9b7e
.\" install.sh and uninstall.sh use this marker to recognize the page.
.TH LSCORE 1 "2026-11-11" "lscore 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lscore \- one-command health check for your Linux machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lscore
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lscore
looks at the machine it runs on and prints a score from 0 to 100 with a letter
grade, a breakdown by category, and the checks that need attention.
It is read-only and offline: it changes nothing on the system, needs no network
access, and sends no telemetry.
It uses only the Python 3 standard library.
.PP
Checks that do not apply to the current machine (for example a battery check on
a desktop) are reported as not applicable and are left out of the score rather
than counted as a pass.
Nothing is printed that could not be determined on this machine.
.PP
By default the run is also appended to a local history file, so
.B \-\-history
can show how the score changed over time.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Output
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a machine-readable JSON report instead of the normal display.
.TP
.BI \-\-card [ FILE ]
Save a shareable SVG card.
The default file name is
.IR lscore-card.svg .
.TP
.B \-\-share
Print a short plain-text summary suitable for pasting into a post or chat.
.TP
.B \-\-badge
Print a Markdown badge for a README.
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Print a shell script with suggested fixes for review.
Nothing is executed.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only the numeric score.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show every check, including the ones that passed or were skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-list-checks
List every check and exit.
With
.B \-\-json
the list is machine-readable.
An explicit
.B \-\-only
or
.B \-\-skip
on the command line narrows the list; filters from the config file do not.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print tracebacks for checks that crash instead of hiding the error.
.SS Selecting checks
.TP
.BI \-\-only " ID"
Run only the named checks or categories.
May be repeated, and accepts comma-separated values.
.TP
.BI \-\-skip " ID"
Skip the named checks or categories.
May be repeated, and accepts comma-separated values.
.SS Comparison and history
.TP
.BI \-\-compare [ FILE ]
Compare this run with an earlier one.
With a
.IR FILE ,
the file must be a report saved by
.BR "lscore \-\-json" .
With no value, the newest entry in the local history file is used.
The comparison adds a section after the normal output; it never changes the
default display.
History entries store the overall score, the number of checks covered and, since
lscore 0.6.0, the category scores, but not per-check results.
Per-check changes are therefore available only when comparing against a saved
.B \-\-json
report that includes check results.
.TP
.B \-\-history
Show recorded scores over time, newest last, with a summary of runs, best,
average, latest, and how long ago the last run was.
.TP
.B \-\-no-history
Do not record this run in the local history file.
.SS Appearance
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Colour theme: 
.B rose
(the pastel default) or
.B basic
(plain 16 colours, easier to read on light terminals).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN"
When to use colour: 
.B auto
(the default), 
.B always
or
.BR never .
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable colour; the same as
.BR "\-\-color never" .
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Use ASCII symbols and rules instead of Unicode.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read defaults from
.IR FILE .
The file must exist and contain an
.B [lscore]
section; otherwise lscore exits with status 2.
.TP
.B \-\-no-config
Ignore the config file for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-completion " SHELL"
Print a completion script for
.BR bash ,
.B zsh
or
.B fish
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.SS Exit status control
.TP
.BI \-\-min " N"
Exit with status 1 if the score is below
.IR N .
Useful in CI.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail-on " LEVEL"
Exit with status 1 when a check of the given severity is present:
.B warn
or
.BR fail .
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
lscore reads optional defaults from
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lscore/config.ini ,
falling back to
.IR ~/.config/lscore/config.ini .
The file is only read; it is never created or modified.
It must contain an
.B [lscore]
section with keys from the list below.
Unknown keys and invalid values produce a warning on standard error and are
ignored.
Command-line flags take precedence over the file, which takes precedence over
the environment and the built-in defaults.
.PP
Keys:
.TP
.B only
Comma-separated checks or categories to run, like
.BR \-\-only .
.TP
.B skip
Comma-separated checks or categories to skip, like
.BR \-\-skip .
.TP
.B min
Integer threshold, like
.BR \-\-min .
.TP
.B fail_on
.B warn
or
.BR fail ,
like
.BR \-\-fail-on .
.TP
.B theme
.B rose
or
.BR basic .
.TP
.B color
.BR auto ,
.B always
or
.BR never .
.TP
.B ascii
Boolean; true is the same as
.BR \-\-ascii .
.TP
.B no_history
Boolean; true is the same as
.BR \-\-no-history .
.PP
Booleans accept
.BR 1/0 ,
.BR true/false ,
.BR yes/no
and
.BR on/off ,
case-insensitively.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lscore/config.ini
Optional configuration (or under
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME ).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/lscore/history.jsonl
Local score history, one JSON object per run (or under
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME ).
The directory is created with mode 0700 and the file with mode 0600, so other
users cannot read it.
It never leaves the machine.
Runs executed as root are not recorded, because a preserved
.B HOME
can leave a root-owned file that normal runs could no longer write.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, colour is disabled in
.B auto
mode, following the usual convention.
.TP
.B LSCORE_THEME
Default theme name when neither a flag nor the config file sets one.
.TP
.B LSCORE_NO_HISTORY
When set to
.BR 1 ,
.BR true ,
.B yes
or
.BR on ,
this run is not recorded.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the optional config file.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for the local history file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, and any
.B \-\-min
or
.B \-\-fail-on
condition was not tripped.
.TP
.B 1
The score was below
.B \-\-min
or a
.B \-\-fail-on
condition was tripped.
.TP
.B 2
An error occurred: bad arguments, an unreadable comparison or config file,
.B \-\-compare
had no recorded run to use, or no check could run on this machine.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B lscore
Show the normal report.
.TP
.B lscore \-\-only security,storage \-\-verbose
Inspect two categories in detail.
.TP
.B lscore \-\-json > before.json
Save a report, then later compare against it:
.B lscore \-\-compare before.json
.TP
.B lscore \-\-compare
Compare with the last recorded run.
.TP
.B lscore \-\-min 80 \-\-fail-on warn
Fail a CI job when the machine drops below 80 or raises a warning.
.TP
.B lscore \-\-no-history \-\-share
Print a shareable summary without recording the run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1)
.PP
Project home and issue tracker: see the README shipped with the source.
